IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ca-traveller`

-- Customs Act 1901 (Cth), with the Customs Regulation 2015 and Customs Tariff Act 1995 Schedule 4 item 15 -- worked cases
-- from the seat of the incoming traveller.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked against a
-- decided case, the Customs By-laws, the Customs (Prohibited Imports) Regulations 1956, or the regulations in force in 2011.
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_customs-act-1901_baseline.py). Expected
-- results were written by hand from the text.
--
-- Facts the lives do not state are ASSUMPTIONS, labelled where used: that a Collector asked for the card (it is handed out
-- on the flight); Chloe's souvenirs (200 dollars) and her parents' purchases; that a carton is 200 cigarettes, so Jake's three
-- cartons are 600; that Jake lodged no Australia Travel Declaration. The By-law figures (25 cigarettes, 900 dollars, as the
-- plan states them; 2,250 mL) are INPUTS, not deposited text. A penalty unit is taken as 330 dollars (the s 4AA figure before
-- indexation) and Jake's duty as 900 dollars: both ILLUSTRATIVE.

