§ `c014 -- Chloe home from Bali, 2011: the card, the concession, nothing to declare`

-- Answered on the 2026 text (the 2011 regulations are not deposited). The biosecurity questions are not here.
#ASSERT `Must I fill in the incoming passenger card` `Chloe, 8, home from Bali (c014, 2011)`

#ASSERT NOT `Do I have anything to declare for customs` `Chloe, 8, home from Bali (c014, 2011)`

#ASSERT NOT `Must I declare my overseas purchases` `Chloe, 8, home from Bali (c014, 2011)`

#ASSERT `Are my other goods within the concession` `Chloe, 8, home from Bali (c014, 2011)` `Concession for Chloe at 8 (no alcohol or tobacco: ASSUMED)`

#ASSERT `Must I enter my goods` TRUE FALSE FALSE 200 FALSE EQUALS `no entry needed: my personal effects (s 68(1)(d))`

#ASSERT NOT `Do I have anything to declare for customs` `Graham, home from Bali with wine and gifts (c014)`
#ASSERT `Do I have anything to declare for customs` `Sue, home from Bali, 950 dollars of purchases (c014 variant)`

§ `k046 -- Jake back from Bali with three cartons, 2031: duty on all but 25, and a false card`

#ASSERT `Must I fill in the incoming passenger card` `Jake, back from Bali with three cartons (k046, 2031)`

#ASSERT `Must I declare my tobacco` `Jake, back from Bali with three cartons (k046, 2031)`

#ASSERT `Do I have anything to declare for customs` `Jake, back from Bali with three cartons (k046, 2031)`

#ASSERT `How many of my cigarettes are duty-free` `Jake, back from Bali with three cartons (k046, 2031)` `Concession for an adult (as the plan states it)` EQUALS 25

#ASSERT `How many cigarettes must I pay duty on` `Jake, back from Bali with three cartons (k046, 2031)` `Concession for an adult (as the plan states it)` EQUALS 575

#ASSERT `Must I enter my goods` TRUE FALSE FALSE 600 TRUE EQUALS `no entry needed: my personal effects (s 68(1)(d))`
#ASSERT `Must I enter my goods` TRUE TRUE FALSE 600 TRUE EQUALS `no entry needed: exempt by reg 25 (value not over 1000 dollars)`
#ASSERT `Must I enter my goods` TRUE TRUE FALSE 1500 TRUE EQUALS `I must enter them for home consumption; tobacco cannot be warehoused (s 68(3))`

#ASSERT `Could my statement be an offence under s 234(1)(d)` `Jake's card: NO to the tobacco question (k046)`
#ASSERT NOT `Could my statement be an offence under s 234(1)(d)` `Jake's card, honestly mistaken (not reckless)`

#ASSERT `Could my statement be an offence under s 243T` `Jake's card: NO to the tobacco question (k046)`
#ASSERT `Could my statement be an offence under s 243T` `Jake's card, honestly mistaken (not reckless)`
#ASSERT NOT `Could my statement be an offence under s 243T` `Jake's card, error notice given and duty paid`
#ASSERT `Could my statement be an offence under s 243T` `Jake's card, error notice given but duty unpaid`
#ASSERT NOT `Could my statement be an offence under s 243T` `Jake's card, uncertainty flagged on it`

#ASSERT NOT `Could my statement be an offence under s 243U` `Jake's card: NO to the tobacco question (k046)`
#ASSERT NOT `Could my statement be an offence under s 243U` `Jake's card, a false answer costing no duty`
#ASSERT `Could my statement be an offence under s 243U` `A false answer about goods that are not accompanied effects, costing no duty`

-- Penalty unit 330 dollars (ASSUMED); duty 900 dollars (ILLUSTRATIVE).
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined under s 234(1)(d)` `Jake's card: NO to the tobacco question (k046)` 900 330 EQUALS 82500
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined under s 234(1)(d)` `A false statement about the amount of duty` 900 330 EQUALS 34800

#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined under s 243T` 900 330 EQUALS 19800
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined under s 243T` 25000 330 EQUALS 25000

#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined under s 243U` 1 330 EQUALS 19800

#ASSERT `What is the most an infringement notice can ask me to pay` 19800 TRUE 330 EQUALS 4950
#ASSERT `What is the most an infringement notice can ask me to pay` 39600 FALSE 330 EQUALS 4950
#ASSERT `What is the most an infringement notice can ask me to pay` 330000 TRUE 330 EQUALS 82500

